 Found accounts already on this PC

 + Imported. To retire claude-acc safely:

 1. Check that Devpit picks the same accounts
    Run `devpit accounts verify`, or open Accounts in a few of the linked folders: Claude Code
    should show the account claude-acc used there.
 2. Remove claude-acc's line from your PowerShell profile
    C:\Users\you\Documents\PowerShell\Microsoft.PowerShell_profile.ps1, line 12:
        Invoke-Expression (& claude-acc init pwsh | Out-String)
    Devpit does not edit your profile; open it with `notepad $PROFILE` and delete the line
    yourself.
 3. Open a new terminal
    claude-acc's line sets CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR every time a terminal changes folder. A terminal
    started after the line is gone has no such variable.
 4. Remove the program
    Delete C:\Users\you\.claude-switch\bin (claude-acc.exe, and claude-acc.old if it is there). If
    you added that folder to PATH yourself, take it out of PATH too.
 5. Keep the account folders
    Devpit uses claude-acc's account folders where they are, so they still hold your sign-ins. Do
    not delete C:\Users\you\.claude-switch\accounts or anything in it while Devpit uses them.
    Do not run `claude-acc remove` for an account you imported: it moves the account's folder to
